# ── admin-frontend build context — was MISSING entirely before this audit. ─────────────────────
# Consequence of the gap: this repo has a real, locally-installed node_modules/ inside
# admin-frontend/ (confirmed: 169 top-level packages on disk at audit time). Without this file,
# the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` in the `builder` stage (Dockerfile line 17) copies that local
# node_modules on top of the one the image had just built two lines earlier via `npm ci`
# (line 10) — the freshly installed Linux-native modules get overwritten by whatever the
# developer's host last had installed. On a Windows dev machine this can inject Windows-only
# native binaries (e.g. platform-specific @rollup/@swc/lightningcss packages) into what is
# supposed to be a linux/amd64 build, silently breaking or corrupting the build. This is a
# correctness bug, not just a context-size one — this file is the fix.

.git
.gitignore
node_modules
dist
build
.env
.env.*
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
coverage
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
